WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:36.080
Half Moon Love

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:54.270
Through the battle against the Alexandria,
Kamille drove back his rival, Jerid Messa.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:02:00.150
The Argama arrived in Von Braun City,
the Moon's neutral city...

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.010
...for replenishments and repairs.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.690
Fa!

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.190
I told you two, you mustn't come here!

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.330
- She's mad again!
- Qum!

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.660
We want to go to Armstrong Plaza.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.190
No way.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.600
Why not take them there?

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.430
You haven't spent much time with them
lately, have you?

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.340
- Now, return to your room!
- We want to go outside!

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.430
No!

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.170
Let's go, Qum.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.380
Fa, go on. Look after them.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.520
Stop crying.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.750
This could be your last opportunity
to play with them, Fa.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.620
Our upcoming operations will be
more intense.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.660
We can't have children aboard with us.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:49.130
That's exactly why I'm too busy right now.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.060
I understand, but...!

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.000
- Hey, where are you going?
- Outside!

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.030
Is Fa taking you out? That's great!

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.980
Von Braun City confirmed. I'm landing.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:24.730
How was the balance after transformation?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.460
Not too good.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.100
But this'll be a great mobile suit.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.100
It's all because of your great skills, Sarah.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:33.840
Where's my stuff?

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.740
Finish the operation by the time limit.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:38.780
Right.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.140
Be careful.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.620
- What's inside?
- Clothes you'll be changing into.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.180
I see.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.550
If I don't return, please move this for me.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:50.790
Understood.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.120
But your priority
is to return safely, all right?

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.160
Right.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:04.600
"Fa's... resolution... as a pilot..."

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.140
Who is it?

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:08.680
It's me!

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.820
I can't find the children.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.750
According to Torres,
they said they were going outside.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.650
Do you know where they might've gone?

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.750
Any place they said they wanted to go?

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.190
They wanted to go to Armstrong Plaza!

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.660
Let's go there.
We can call in later.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:48.710
<i>You can go straight to the Argama</i>
<i>from Armstrong Plaza?</i>

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.290
<i>To escape, I'll leave from there</i>
<i>and turn left.</i>

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:53.580
Okay, then.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.180
Kamille... Bidan.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.300
Hello.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.540
What is it, Kamille?

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.970
- Well...!
- What?

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.170
I'd like to try this on. May I?

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.110
Yourself, Miss?

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:52.770
I've always wanted to try it on.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.520
Please bring it over.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:56.850
Right away.

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.750
What are you doing, Kamille?

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.850
- Must be my imagination.
- You're talking to yourself.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:04.860
I was curious how these clothes
would look on you, Fa.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.690
We're here to look for Shinta and Qum!

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.030
Sorry to keep you.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:16.300
- You wanted to try this on?
- R-Right.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:21.040
But looking closer, I think it's a little
too mature for me.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.310
Sorry!

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.980
<i>Kamille's here.</i>

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.420
<i>Why is it?</i>

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.290
<i>Once I'm aware of his presence,</i>
<i>I feel quite uncomfortable.</i>

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.860
I hear it again.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.060
Could it be Four?

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.070
Kamille! Did you find them over there?!

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.070
Nobody here has seen them either!

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.440
What'll we do?

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:57.140
Why don't you search here a little more,
and then return by car.

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:59.270
- I'll go back the way we came.
- Okay.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.750
I have one more hour.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:14.190
<i>All passengers boarding</i>
<i>the flight to Granada...</i>

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:15.890
<i>...please proceed to Gate 5.</i>

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.730
This is not the way to the gates.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.800
What? But they said it's this way.

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:25.940
Gate 5, right?

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.080
That's right.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:05.480
Is Four here?

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:11.980
<i>The gate to board the flight</i>
<i>to Granada is now closed.</i>

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.480
Why, you're...

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:16.530
Sarah!

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:19.660
Stop there!

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.100
Hey!

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.740
What are you doing here?!

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:32.230
Sarah Zabiarov!

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:33.530
Let go of me!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.670
I promise I won't run away.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:41.410
I was hoping for the chance
to talk with you. Just the two of us.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:43.050
Then why did you run away?!

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.410
Because I got scared!

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.990
Don't look at me that way!

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.950
I felt you were a dangerous person!

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.660
You're kidding! Others never say I'm...!

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:58.220
Once they find out I'm a young pilot,
they say I'm conceited and...

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.240
...that as a Newtype, I should be
with the A.E.U.G..

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:06.610
But you ran after me,
as if you meant to scold me.

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:08.770
I didn't mean to...!

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.050
What a beautiful place.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.640
I can't believe we're on the Moon.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.960
- Where are we going?
- Wherever you like.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.460
How am I different from those girls?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.790
Nobody thinks of me as a girl.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:34.400
No matter what clothes I wear.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:36.410
Sarah.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.370
Kamille.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.170
If you don't like it, then quit.

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.270
Quit what?

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:46.580
Quit who you are.
You should become an ordinary girl.

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.670
Enjoy some ice cream
and chat with friends.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:50.450
I can't do that!

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.420
How do you know unless you try?!

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.460
- It's impossible!
- It's not impossible!

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:56.860
Kamille!

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:58.660
- Two ice creams.
- Coming up.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:01.660
What are you doing?!

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:04.600
Isn't that the girl who
infiltrated the Argama?

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.290
I'm not sure what,
but something's not right.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.070
Can't you give me a straight answer?

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:11.110
Here you are!

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.250
So what do you plan to do, Kamille?

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.040
Fa, you'd better return first.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.340
But...!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.980
I feel there's something strange going on.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:25.420
Will you be okay?

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:28.360
Fa, I want you to return
and let Captain Bright know.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:30.590
Kamille.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:38.270
<i>Why am I waiting here as if</i>
<i>I were anxious to see him?</i>

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.170
Sarah! I'm glad you waited for me.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.710
This is the first time I've ever sat
back and eaten like this.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:01.350
Really? You've got to learn
to enjoy your youth.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:02.910
Like everyone else.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.550
I see.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:06.560
Why are you being so kind to me?

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.790
Let's see.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:13.390
Because you remind me
of someone I met sometime back.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.330
Your girlfriend?

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:19.500
I hope she feels that way.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:30.420
Do you remember when I asked you
whether you're a Cyber-Newtype or not?

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:35.250
That time you tested me, right?

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:39.060
Because of you,
Katz no longer trusts anyone.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.730
So I don't want to
ever see you again!

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.170
Not even in battle!

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:46.700
Otherwise, I'll tear you to pieces!

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:50.600
But I met Scirocco before you!

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.440
It can't be helped!

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:14.960
Goodbye, Sarah!

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.920
Wait, where are you going?!

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.300
I'm returning to the Argama!

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:21.100
I suggest you also return to your unit!

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.640
No, Kamille!
You mustn't return to the Argama!

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.600
I mustn't return to the Argama?!

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:27.730
Not now!

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:28.780
Why not?!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.370
Why mustn't I return to the Argama?!

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.310
B-Because... because...

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.410
...it's dangerous!

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:38.890
I can't understand why returning to
my own ship would be dangerous!

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:39.940
Why?!

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:40.780
Because...

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.320
...this plaza and the spaceport...
It's all going to disappear.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:45.820
You bitch!

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:47.860
How could you?!

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:51.300
I set a time bomb
in the spaceport's pipe room.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:55.160
- The spaceport's pipe room?
- Of Gate 5.

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:56.330
Okay!

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:57.770
- It's useless!
- Why?!

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:01.300
You don't know where the bomb is
in the air pipes, do you?!

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:04.010
- When does the bomb go off?!
- Four o'clock.

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:06.010
I have thirty minutes!

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:07.910
Those must be your tools!

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:09.010
K-Kamille!

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.550
Excuse me!
Please let me use the microphone!

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.390
The microphone?!

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:16.930
I'm with the Forces. Hurry!

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:18.360
- But...!
- Excuse me.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:21.620
Petty Officer Fa!
Call the Plaza's PA room at once!

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:26.030
<i>Petty Officer Fa!
Call the PA room at once!</i>

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:28.360
It's Kamille.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.710
Hello. Oh, Kamille?
What's wrong?

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:38.300
Tell Captain Bright to launch
the Argama immediately.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.540
Huh?! Why?!

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:41.050
A bomb has been set!

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:43.080
I'm told it'll go off at four!

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:46.750
That girl told you, didn't she?!
Did she set the bomb?!

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:48.880
We need to verify the information!

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:52.720
We need to give out an evacuation
order to the spaceport and plaza...

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.230
...but consult with the captain first!

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.360
I'm going to look for the bomb!

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.600
You're coming with me, Sarah.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:01.970
You'll never make it.
You'd be wise to escape.

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.030
You're to follow the Argama's orders!
Got that?!

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:05.500
B-But...!

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:07.700
Open a direct line to the Argama!

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.440
I'll be in the Gate 5 pipe room.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:24.280
It looks like the Radish was able to hold
more mobile suits than we estimated.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:27.590
With this, we should be able to stop
the Titans from dropping colonies.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:32.400
In the meantime, we must pursue
the battleship that left from Axis.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.260
Captain Bright!

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.200
This place will explode!

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:38.130
What do you mean?!

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:39.730
It's a message from Kamille.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:43.270
Apparently a time bomb has been set
near the spaceport gate.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:45.180
A bomb?!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:48.450
He wants you to connect online
with the plaza's information center!

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.880
Where's Kamille?!

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.520
He's searching for the bomb.

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.580
Sarah, who set the bomb,
is also with him!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:56.420
Saegusa!

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.050
Get the Hyaku Shiki onboard...

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.720
...and get in touch with Mr. Wong
and Lieutenant Quattro!

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:01.730
Yes, sir!

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:02.790
- Fa!
- Yes!

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:06.730
Regardless of the panic it may cause,
an evacuation order should be given.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.670
The one beside it is the oil pipeline.

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:13.610
That's very clever,
to detonate the whole pipeline.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:16.780
This way, I can spread fire
through the whole spaceport...

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.310
...with a small amount of explosives.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.650
Okay, it's open.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.390
It's stuck!

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.520
I've got twenty minutes.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.160
I almost have it.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.100
Kamille...?

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:49.700
I failed.

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:51.370
You did the best you could, Kamille.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.850
We'd better get out of here quickly.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.180
Goodbye, Kamille.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:58.980
You're not getting away!

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.550
If I must die, you're coming with me!

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.620
The evacuation notice has been given!
We'll leave, too!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:09.820
Get me an electric car!

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.660
I need you to get me a car.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:12.700
Y-Yes!

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:30.580
<i>This girl had every chance</i>
<i>to run away if she wanted to, but she didn't.</i>

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.890
<i>She's no Cyber-Newtype.</i>

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.330
<i>There's something very normal about her.</i>

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:46.020
Apolly, over here!

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:49.570
<i>Get on! We have no time!</i>

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.230
Three minutes! Engine, maximum output!

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:53.870
You got Kamille?

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:54.910
Good!

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.240
Proceed to the spaceport exit hatch!

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:58.550
Roger!

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:04.280
We made it!

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:06.590
<i>Okay, they're in!</i>

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:14.990
<i>We're unsure of the size of the explosion!</i>

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:17.760
Do everything you can to put out the fire
in Von Braun City!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.470
That's right!

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.770
The fire will spread from Gate 5!

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:25.930
It's time.

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:52.930
The Argama has launched.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.200
<i>I'm worried about Sarah. Let's go in.</i>

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.140
The mechanic can't pilot the Messala,
can he?

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.370
<i>If I just need to follow you,</i>
<i>then no problem!</i>

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:00.540
Okay!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:03.610
Fa, don't get yourself down!

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:07.010
I just know that both Shinta and Qum
were engulfed in that explosion!

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:09.850
- <i>Enemy craft detected!</i>
- They were around after all!

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:13.850
So, this was your plan
right from the beginning?!

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.290
Of course it was!

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.520
I'm Mr. Paptimus's soldier!

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:20.090
Then why did you co-operate
with me earlier?!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.390
Something was wrong with me.

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:27.300
You're not the kind of person
who should work for Scirocco!

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.300
Listen, stay here! Got that?!

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:35.270
Kamille, you don't know how kind
Mr. Paptimus is.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:46.220
Fa, we're going! Be careful!

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:48.380
Yes! Methuss, taking off!

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.320
What?! This mobile suit!

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.200
They're here!

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:05.000
How dare he...?

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:06.370
Zeta Gundam, taking off!

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:14.350
Starboard, hit by beam!

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:17.350
- Fire fighting unit!
- Closing shutters to Path 8!

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:43.400
Just because you're in a new model...!

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.420
Methuss! Rick Dias! Sandwich the enemy!

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:01.430
Kamille! There it goes!

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:04.930
I can get it.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:07.090
Over there?!

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:11.400
It's that girl!

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:13.030
Qum and Shinta were killed
all because of her!

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:20.440
Fa! What are you doing?!

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:24.520
Sarah's flying!

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.580
Sarah is flying?!

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:32.920
How could she?!

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.960
<i>The ice cream was delicious, wasn't it?</i>

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:44.570
You can't live your life
on the other side!

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:50.710
Sarah.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:54.950
Th-That's crazy.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:57.040
You know very well.

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.050
Why do you submit yourself
to be ruined?!

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:15.270
The Argama's proceeding with plans
without receiving repairs?

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:18.070
Yeah, we were told to make repairs
en route.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:19.730
That's got to be tough.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:42.490
You two...?!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.330
- You found us!
- Why?!

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:50.930
We both hate taking baths...

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:53.670
...so we thought you would never
come here to look for us.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.540
What made you decide to hide?!

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:59.570
Because we don't want to say
goodbye to you, Fa!

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:02.980
You two... you two...!

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:09.220
You'd better not try
something like this again!

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:24.270
The Argama leaves the Moon without
getting a chance to repair its damages.

00:22:24.340 --> 00:22:26.860
From the asteroid belt comes Axis.

00:22:26.940 --> 00:22:31.570
And from Axis comes one battleship,
headed for the Earth Sphere.

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:35.250
The Argama plans to make contact
with the battleship.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:49.200
Yazan forces the Argama to the brink...

00:23:49.270 --> 00:23:51.210
...just as Scirocco had hoped.

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:54.810
However, a mobile suit team comes to
the Argama's rescue...

00:23:54.880 --> 00:23:56.850
...forcing Yazan's unit back.

00:23:57.080 --> 00:24:01.380
Nobody notices that Char bites
his lip in frustration.

00:24:01.850 --> 00:24:06.810
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Unidentified Mobile Suits".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Unidentified Mobile Suits

00:24:07.490 --> 00:24:10.060
You will see the tears of time.
